id:                     DRAFT-7353
trigger_tool:           clang|ld|cmake|conan_test
phase:                  test_package|build|linking
error_signature:        use of undeclared identifier 'BLANK'|
                         use of undeclared identifier 'KEY_DELETE'|
                         use of undeclared identifier 'KEY_LEFT_CONTROL'|
                         use of undeclared identifier 'KEY_HOME'|
                         initializing 'Vector2' \(aka 'struct Vector2'\) with an expression of incompatible type 'int'|
                         static declaration of 'MeasureTextEx' follows non-static declaration|
                         conflicting types for 'GetMouseWheelMove'|
                         passing 'int' to parameter of incompatible type 'Color'|
                         too many arguments provided to function-like macro invocation|
                         undefined symbol: RL_FREE|
                         undefined symbol: GetGlyphIndex|
                         undefined symbol: GetCodepoint|
                         undefined symbol: DrawTextCodepoint|
                         undefined symbol: UnloadTexture|
                         undefined symbol: GetScreenWidth

severity:               2
category:               linking, platform, api
match_keywords:         RAYGUI_STANDALONE, RAYGUI_IMPLEMENTATION, header-only, raygui,
                         BLANK, KEY_DELETE, GetMouseWheelMove, GetCharPressed, LoadFileText,
                         MeasureTextEx, RL_FREE, GetGlyphIndex, GetCodepoint, DrawTextCodepoint,
                         GetScreenWidth, UnloadTexture, standalone backend, incomplete type forward declaration
title:                  Header-only GUI library that calls a host backend fails consumer test on host-less platform

root_cause:             A header-only GUI library guarded by a backend mode switch (raygui.h with
                         RAYGUI_STANDALONE) omits its host header (raylib.h) when the switch is set, so every
                         host symbol its implementation section touches must be supplied by the consumer.
                         The library's own STANDALONE declaration block only covers a subset: color macros
                         (BLANK/GRAY/...), extra key codes (KEY_DELETE/KEY_HOME/KEY_END/KEY_INSERT/
                         KEY_LEFT_SHIFT/KEY_LEFT_CONTROL), the RL_FREE allocator macro and host functions
                         (Fade/MeasureTextEx/GetScreenWidth/GetGlyphIndex/GetCodepoint/DrawTextCodepoint/
                         UnloadTexture) are called without any declaration. They surface one round at a
                         time: undeclared identifier at compile time, implicit-int declarations that
                         collide with the user's typed definitions (initializing Vector2 with int,
                         conflicting types, static follows non-static), then undefined symbols at link
                         time. An upstream changelog may even claim a dependency was removed while one
                         call site survives (raygui 4.0 MeasureTextEx in the tooltip path).

affected_scope:         Header-only libraries whose implementation calls a host-platform backend behind a
                         mode switch (raygui RAYGUI_STANDALONE, nuklear-style pluggable backends) when the
                         consumer platform lacks the host (OHOS without raylib/X11), typically in a Conan
                         test_package that must compile the implementation TU to be a real test.

verification_cmd:       conan create with test_package compiling RAYGUI_IMPLEMENTATION+RAYGUI_STANDALONE TU and asserting pure-logic APIs (GuiGetState/GuiIsLocked/GuiGetStyle roundtrip)

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           standalone-header-backend-completion
rec_description:        Three-part backend completion, all BEFORE and AFTER a single include of the
                         library header. (1) Before the include: define the host color macros (26),
                         missing key codes, the allocator macro (RL_FREE -> free, matching the
                         RAYGUI_MALLOC/CALLOC default), forward typedefs of the library's own structs as
                         INCOMPLETE types (typedef struct Color Color; etc. — completed later inside the
                         header, legal repeated typedef), and prototypes for every host function the
                         implementation calls that the header itself does not declare. This kills
                         implicit-int declarations in one pass instead of iterating error by error.
                         (2) Keep function-like helper macros OUT of the pre-include block when call
                         sites pass compound literals — a Fade(color, alpha) macro breaks on braces
                         (too many arguments); declare a prototype instead. (3) After the include, define
                         stubs matching the library's STANDALONE declaration block signatures exactly
                         (raygui 4.0: GetMouseWheelMove returns float, GetCharPressed not GetKeyPressed,
                         LoadFileText not LoadText, plus LoadTextureFromImage/SetShapesTexture/
                         LoadCodepoints/UnloadCodepoints/DecompressData/UnloadFileText); define surviving
                         host-call sites (MeasureTextEx) as non-static to match the implicit declaration
                         ordering, and keep them in the same TU. Then assert pure-logic APIs (GuiGetState,
                         GuiIsLocked, GuiSetStyle/GuiGetStyle roundtrip, GuiIconText) that need no
                         rendering, so the test exercises the real compiled implementation.
rec_command:            grep the header for undeclared host symbols before writing stubs: grep -oE "\b(Fade|GetColor|GetScreenWidth|GetGlyphIndex|GetCodepoint|DrawTextCodepoint|UnloadTexture|RL_FREE|KEY_[A-Z_]+)\b" raygui.h | sort -u, then diff against the STANDALONE declaration block
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               test-package-backend-stubs

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      report-env-unsupported-or-header-only-distribution
fallback_description:  If the library has no backend switch and hard-requires the host runtime, do not
                         fake a test: distribute as header-only (package_type header-library) and either
                         consume with a minimal implementation TU only when the backend seam exists, or
                         report env_unsupported when no real API can run without the host.
fallback_command:       inspect the header for a backend/mode switch before committing to a consumer test
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          adaptation-scope-decision

forbid_1_pattern:       printf.*PASSED|pass-only|include-only test
forbid_1_reason:        A test that only includes the header or prints a string never compiles the
                         implementation TU, hiding every backend symbol issue this entry describes.
forbid_1_consequence:   CI green while real consumers cannot build against the package.

forbid_2_pattern:       patch .*raygui\.h|edit upstream header to remove host calls
forbid_2_reason:        Rewriting the upstream header to drop backend calls diverges the package from
                         upstream semantics and violates the patch-minimality rule.
forbid_2_consequence:   Package behavior drifts from upstream; every upstream update breaks the patch.

